{"orgCode":"0160","name":"Legislative Counsel Bureau","agencyCode":"0010","agencyName":"Legislative, Judicial, and Executive","description":"The Legislative Counsel Bureau (Bureau) provides legal services to the two houses of the Legislature, and their members and committees, by resolving a large volume of complex legal problems arising in connection with the legislative process. The legal services furnished include rendering legal opinions, drafting bills and other legislative measures, counseling, attending meetings of legislative committees as counsel, and representing the Legislature in litigation. The Bureau also provides legal services to the Governor and advises state agencies as to the preparation of legislative measures. An attorney-client relationship is maintained and all work is confidential.\n\nThe Bureau prepares indices and appropriate tables necessary to identify legislative measures and compiles and indexes statutes and codes.\n\nThe Bureau also operates the Legislative Data Center, which provides technology services to the Legislature, including IT services in support of legislative business operations and the legislative information system, which provides information to the public regarding pending legislation and existing law.\n\nPursuant to Chapter 46 of the Statutes of 2012, the California Commission on Uniform State Laws was transferred into the Bureau. The California Commission on Uniform State Laws presents to the Legislature uniform laws recommended by the National Conference of Commissioners on Uniform State Laws and then promotes passage of these uniform acts.\n\nPursuant to Chapter 450 of the Statutes of 2018, the Bureau provides advice and investigation services to the Legislature related to workplace misconduct through the Workplace Conduct Unit.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":180449,"cy":198264,"by":185033},"positions":{"py":567.5,"cy":659,"by":659},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":142,"cy":131,"by":131},"nongovernmental":{"py":33211,"cy